// Northwind's own write, reached from the PACK's own shopper form.
//
// This file is the half of the section 7 claim that did not exist until the
// shopper-form extension did (design record 2026-09-21). The concept beside
// it declared an EIN and an @relationship to the pack's application, exactly
// as the design prescribes -- and nothing could ever write a row of it. A
// pack declares its shopper form in Go; a client repository ships no Go; and
// the bff drops an undeclared input by design. So "client-specific fields
// are a related concept, not a blob" was true of the SCHEMA and false of
// every path a field could actually travel.
//
// @shopperFormExtension is that path. It adds Northwind's fields to the
// route the pack already opened -- it does not open one, and could not: a
// public endpoint on a merchant's origin stays the privilege of Go compiled
// into the engine.
//
// THE THREE STAMPED NAMES ARE DECLARED AND NEVER OFFERED. submissionId and
// storeId are in the args block so this body can write them, and the
// registry refuses either as a field a shopper may send. submissionId is
// the id the bff minted for this submission and the id the pack wrote its
// application at, which is what makes the @relationship point at a row that
// exists.
//
// siteId is deliberately NOT declared: it is provenance, and the
// application this row relates to already carries it. A field this concept
// does not have is a field it does not take.

@shopperFormExtension(pack="wholesale", form="application")
mutation northwindTaxDetail recordNorthwindTaxDetail {
  args {
    submissionId  string!
    storeId       string!
    ein           string!  @maxLength(20)
  }
  insert {
    accept { ein }
    stamp {
      id:            args.submissionId
      applicationId: args.submissionId
      storeId:       args.storeId
      ownerUserId:   actor.userId
    }
  }
}
